from the clipboard"},"198":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-29","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#pasting-and-dropping-images","content":"Pick image files from disk"},"199":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-30","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#pasting-and-dropping-images","content":"Drag and drop image files into the canvas"},"200":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-31","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#pasting-and-dropping-images","content":"Supported image types include PNG, JPG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, SVG, and BMP. Images become Excalidraw image elements, so you can draw around them, resize them, and annotate them before sending."},"201":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-32","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#sending-to-the-agent","content":"When you click **Send**, Gent exports the current board as `image/png`, writes a temporary file, closes the drawing modal, and attaches that one PNG to the agent message."},"202":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-33","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#sending-to-the-agent","content":"This keeps the chat input simple: the agent receives one visual artifact that contains the sketch, pasted images, arrows, labels, and annotations together."},"203":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-34","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#autosave-and-history","content":"Draw autosaves non-empty scenes and stores a thumbnail for history. Use the History control to reopen previous drawings, continue editing them, or delete old entries."},"204":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-35","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#autosave-and-history","content":"Autosave stores the Excalidraw scene data so reopening a drawing keeps editable elements, not just a flat screenshot."},"205":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-36","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#exporting-without-sending","content":"Use **Export** when you want to save the drawing locally but not send it to the agent. Gent writes a PNG to the location you choose."},"206":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-37","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#draw-vs-canvas","content":"Surface"},"207":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-38","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#draw-vs-canvas","content":"Best for"},"208":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-39","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#draw-vs-canvas","content":"Gent Draw"},"209":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-40","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#draw-vs-canvas","content":"Human sketches, annotations, pasted screenshots, and visual prompts"},"210":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-41","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#draw-vs-canvas","content":"Gent Canvas"},"211":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-42","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#draw-vs-canvas","content":"Agent-generated HTML, charts, prototypes, demos, and interactive web artifacts"},"212":{"id":"/docs/features/draw-43","page_id":"/docs/features/draw","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/draw#draw-vs-canvas","content":"Use Draw when the human needs to communicate visually. Use Canvas when the agent needs to render something visual."},"213":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","type":"page","content":"File Transfer","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/file-transfer"},"214":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-0","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/file-transfer","content":"Send and receive files between paired devices."},"215":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-1","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#sending-files","content":"Sending files"},"216":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-2","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#open-the-send-tab","content":"Open the Send tab"},"217":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-3","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#select-files","content":"Select files"},"218":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-4","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#pick-a-destination","content":"Pick a destination"},"219":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-5","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#send","content":"Send"},"220":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-6","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#receiving-files","content":"Receiving files"},"221":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-7","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"222":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-8","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#supported-file-types","content":"Supported file types"},"223":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-9","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/file-transfer","content":"Gent includes built-in file transfer between paired devices. Send files from your desktop to your phone, or receive files from your phone to your desktop — no third-party apps, cloud services, or cables needed."},"224":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-10","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#open-the-send-tab","content":"Navigate to the send interface in Gent."},"225":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-11","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#select-files","content":"Choose one or more files from your device. You can select multiple files at once."},"226":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-12","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#pick-a-destination","content":"Select the paired device you want to send to from the device list."},"227":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-13","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#send","content":"The files transfer directly over your local network. Large files transfer quickly since there is no cloud relay — data goes straight from device to device."},"228":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-14","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#receiving-files","content":"When a paired device sends you files, Gent notifies you and shows the incoming transfer. Received files are saved to your configured download location."},"229":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-15","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#how-it-works","content":"File transfers use the same direct TCP connection as all other Gent features. Files travel directly between devices on your local network with no intermediate server. Transfer speeds are limited only by your local network bandwidth — typically much faster than cloud-based alternatives."},"230":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-16","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#how-it-works","content":"File transfer works between any two paired devices: desktop to phone, phone to desktop, or desktop to desktop."},"231":{"id":"/docs/features/file-transfer-17","page_id":"/docs/features/file-transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/file-transfer#supported-file-types","content":"Any file type is supported. There are no restrictions on what you can send — documents, images, videos, code archives, binaries, or anything else."},"232":{"id":"/docs/features/ide","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","type":"page","content":"IDE","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/ide"},"233":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-0","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide","content":"Built-in multi-file editor with file tree, git integration, and syntax highlighting."},"234":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-1","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/ide#opening-the-ide","content":"Opening the IDE"},"235":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-2","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/ide#file-tree","content":"File tree"},"236":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-3","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/ide#editor","content":"Editor"},"237":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-4","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/ide#single-file-editor","content":"Single-file editor"},"238":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-5","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/ide#remote-editing","content":"Remote editing"},"239":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-6","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/ide#file-browser","content":"File browser"},"240":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-7","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide","content":"Gent includes a built-in IDE for editing code without leaving the app. It is not a replacement for VS Code or JetBrains — it is a lightweight, always-available editor that is especially useful when you are working remotely from your phone or tablet."},"241":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-8","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#opening-the-ide","content":"Click &#x2A;*+** in the tab bar"},"242":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-9","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#opening-the-ide","content":"Select **IDE**"},"243":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-10","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#opening-the-ide","content":"Choose a folder to open"},"244":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-11","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#opening-the-ide","content":"The IDE shows a file tree on the left and an editor pane on the right. Click any file to open it."},"245":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-12","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#file-tree","content":"The file tree is git-aware. It uses `git ls-files` to list tracked files, which means it automatically respects your `.gitignore` and skips build artifacts, `node_modules`, and other ignored directories. For non-git projects, it falls back to a standard directory listing."},"246":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-13","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#file-tree","content":"You can:"},"247":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-14","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#file-tree","content":"Navigate folders by expanding/collapsing them"},"248":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-15","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#file-tree","content":"Open files by clicking"},"249":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-16","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#file-tree","content":"Search files by name using the search bar at the top of the tree"},"250":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-17","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#editor","content":"The editor supports syntax highlighting for 100+ languages through the re\\_editor package. Features include:"},"251":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-18","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#editor","content":"Syntax highlighting with language auto-detection based on file extension"},"252":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-19","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#editor","content":"Line numbers"},"253":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-20","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#editor","content":"Find and replace"},"254":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-21","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#editor","content":"Undo/redo"},"255":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-22","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#editor","content":"Standard keyboard shortcuts for editing"},"256":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-23","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#editor","content":"The IDE is designed for quick edits and code review, not as a full development environment. For heavy editing sessions, pair it with your preferred desktop editor and use Gent's IDE for on-the-go changes."},"257":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-24","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#single-file-editor","content":"If you just need to edit one file without a full project tree, use the **Editor** tab type instead. It opens a single file in an editor with the same syntax highlighting and editing features."},"258":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-25","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#remote-editing","content":"The IDE works from paired remote devices. When you open an IDE tab on a remote session, you are browsing and editing files on the desktop. Changes are saved directly to the desktop's filesystem."},"259":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-26","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#remote-editing","content":"This is particularly useful for:"},"260":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-27","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#remote-editing","content":"Quick fixes from your phone while away from your desk"},"261":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-28","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#remote-editing","content":"Reviewing code that an AI agent just modified"},"262":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-29","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#remote-editing","content":"Editing configuration files on a remote machine"},"263":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-30","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#file-browser","content":"The file browser modal lets you navigate your filesystem to find files or folders. It supports:"},"264":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-31","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#file-browser","content":"Breadcrumb navigation"},"265":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-32","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#file-browser","content":"Quick search with fuzzy matching"},"266":{"id":"/docs/features/ide-33","page_id":"/docs/features/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/ide#file-browser","content":"Git-aware file listing that filters out ignored files"},"267":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","type":"page","content":"Orchestrator","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/orchestrator"},"268":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-0","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator","content":"Run multiple AI agents in parallel with the multi-agent orchestrator."},"269":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-1","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"270":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-2","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#use-cases","content":"Use cases"},"271":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-3","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#creating-a-run","content":"Creating a run"},"272":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-4","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#open-the-orchestrator","content":"Open the Orchestrator"},"273":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-5","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#define-your-tasks","content":"Define your tasks"},"274":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-6","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#start-the-run","content":"Start the run"},"275":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-7","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#monitor-and-review","content":"Monitor and review"},"276":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-8","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#task-states","content":"Task states"},"277":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-9","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#concurrency","content":"Concurrency"},"278":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-10","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#retries","content":"Retries"},"279":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-11","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator","content":"The Orchestrator lets you run multiple AI agent sessions in parallel, coordinated by a plan. Instead of sending tasks to one agent at a time, you define a set of tasks and the orchestrator distributes them across concurrent agent sessions, tracks progress, and handles retries."},"280":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-12","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#how-it-works","content":"The orchestrator follows a straightforward model:"},"281":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-13","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#how-it-works","content":"**Define tasks** — describe what needs to be done, broken into independent units of work"},"282":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-14","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#how-it-works","content":"**Create a run** — the orchestrator schedules tasks and assigns them to agent sessions"},"283":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-15","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#how-it-works","content":"**Monitor progress** — watch as agents work in parallel, with real-time status updates"},"284":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-16","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#how-it-works","content":"**Review results** — see what each agent accomplished when the run completes"},"285":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-17","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#how-it-works","content":"Each task runs in its own agent chat session. The orchestrator manages the lifecycle — starting sessions, sending prompts, monitoring for completion, and handling failures with automatic retries."},"286":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-18","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#use-cases","content":"**Large refactors**: Split a codebase-wide change into file-by-file or module-by-module tasks"},"287":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-19","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#use-cases","content":"**Parallel code reviews**: Have multiple agents review different parts of a PR simultaneously"},"288":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-20","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#use-cases","content":"**Batch operations**: Run the same type of task across many files or repositories"},"289":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-21","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#use-cases","content":"**Testing campaigns**: Generate tests for multiple modules in parallel"},"290":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-22","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#open-the-orchestrator","content":"Click &#x2A;*+** in the tab bar and select **Orchestrator**."},"291":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-23","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#define-your-tasks","content":"Add tasks with descriptions of what each agent should do. Each task should be independent — agents work in parallel without knowledge of what other agents are doing."},"292":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-24","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#start-the-run","content":"The orchestrator creates agent chat sessions for each task and begins execution. You can watch progress in real time."},"293":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-25","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#monitor-and-review","content":"Each task shows its status: pending, running, completed, or failed. Failed tasks are retried automatically with exponential backoff."},"294":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-26","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#monitor-and-review","content":"Tasks should be independent units of work. The orchestrator runs them in parallel, so tasks that depend on each other's output will not work well. Design your tasks so each agent can work without waiting for another."},"295":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-27","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#task-states","content":"State"},"296":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-28","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#task-states","content":"Meaning"},"297":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-29","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#task-states","content":"Pending"},"298":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-30","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#task-states","content":"Queued, waiting for an available agent session"},"299":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-31","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#task-states","content":"Running"},"300":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-32","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#task-states","content":"An agent is actively working on this task"},"301":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-33","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#task-states","content":"Completed"},"302":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-34","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#task-states","content":"The agent finished successfully"},"303":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-35","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#task-states","content":"Failed"},"304":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-36","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#task-states","content":"The task failed — will be retried up to the configured limit"},"305":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-37","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#concurrency","content":"The orchestrator manages how many agent sessions run simultaneously. This prevents overwhelming your machine with too many concurrent CLI processes. Tasks that exceed the concurrency limit are queued and start as earlier tasks complete."},"306":{"id":"/docs/features/orchestrator-38","page_id":"/docs/features/orchestrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/orchestrator#retries","content":"When a task fails, the orchestrator retries it with exponential backoff. This handles transient issues like API rate limits or temporary network errors. You can configure the maximum number of retries per task."},"307":{"id":"/docs/features/projects","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","type":"page","content":"Projects","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/projects"},"308":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-0","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects","content":"Organize terminals, editors, and agent chats into project workspaces."},"309":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-1","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/projects#creating-a-project","content":"Creating a project"},"310":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-2","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/projects#what-projects-contain","content":"What projects contain"},"311":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-3","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/projects#working-directory","content":"Working directory"},"312":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-4","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/projects#switching-between-projects","content":"Switching between projects"},"313":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-5","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/projects#when-to-use-projects","content":"When to use projects"},"314":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-6","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects","content":"Projects let you group related sessions together. Instead of having a flat list of terminal tabs, editor tabs, and agent chats, you can organize them by project — keeping your frontend work separate from your backend work, or your personal projects separate from work."},"315":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-7","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#creating-a-project","content":"Click &#x2A;*+** in the tab bar"},"316":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-8","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#creating-a-project","content":"Select **Project**"},"317":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-9","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#creating-a-project","content":"Choose a working directory for the project"},"318":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-10","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#creating-a-project","content":"The project opens as a container tab. Inside it, you can create terminals, editors, and agent chats that are scoped to that project's directory."},"319":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-11","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#what-projects-contain","content":"A project can hold:"},"320":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-12","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#what-projects-contain","content":"**Terminals** that start in the project's working directory"},"321":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-13","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#what-projects-contain","content":"**Agent chats** scoped to the project's codebase"},"322":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-14","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#what-projects-contain","content":"**IDE tabs** that open the project's folder"},"323":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-15","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#what-projects-contain","content":"**Web previews** for dev servers running in the project"},"324":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-16","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#working-directory","content":"Every session created within a project inherits the project's working directory. When you open a new terminal inside a project, it starts in the project root. When you start an agent chat, the AI assistant has context about the project's files."},"325":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-17","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#working-directory","content":"This means you do not need to `cd` into your project directory every time you open a new terminal — the project handles that for you."},"326":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-18","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#switching-between-projects","content":"Projects appear as tabs in the main tab bar, just like terminals and editors. Click a project tab to switch to it and see its sessions."},"327":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-19","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#switching-between-projects","content":"Projects are a local organizational tool. They do not create any files in your project directory or modify your repository in any way."},"328":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-20","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#when-to-use-projects","content":"Projects are most useful when you are working on multiple codebases at once. Instead of managing a sea of unlabeled terminal tabs, you can group everything by context:"},"329":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-21","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#when-to-use-projects","content":"**Monorepo work**: One project for the frontend, another for the backend, another for infrastructure"},"330":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-22","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#when-to-use-projects","content":"**Multi-repo development**: Separate projects for related but distinct repositories"},"331":{"id":"/docs/features/projects-23","page_id":"/docs/features/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/projects#when-to-use-projects","content":"**Context switching**: Keep your side project's sessions separate from your work sessions"},"332":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","type":"page","content":"Terminal","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/terminal"},"333":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-0","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal","content":"Full PTY terminal emulation with tabs, scrollback, and remote access."},"334":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-1","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/terminal#local-terminals","content":"Local terminals"},"335":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-2","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/terminal#what-works","content":"What works"},"336":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-3","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/terminal#remote-terminals","content":"Remote terminals"},"337":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-4","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/terminal#working-with-multiple-terminals","content":"Working with multiple terminals"},"338":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-5","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/terminal#terminal-within-projects","content":"Terminal within projects"},"339":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-6","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal","content":"Gent's terminal is a real PTY shell — not a simplified command runner. It uses full xterm emulation backed by a native PTY, so everything you expect from a terminal works: colors, cursor addressing, interactive programs, shell completion, and full Unicode support."},"340":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-7","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#local-terminals","content":"A local terminal runs your default shell (zsh, bash, fish, or whatever you have configured) directly on the machine. Each terminal tab is an independent session with its own working directory and environment."},"341":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-8","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#local-terminals","content":"You can open as many terminal tabs as you need. Each one is a separate shell process."},"342":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-9","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#what-works","content":"Full ANSI color and formatting (256-color and truecolor)"},"343":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-10","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#what-works","content":"Interactive programs: `vim`, `nano`, `top`, `htop`, `less`, and more"},"344":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-11","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#what-works","content":"Shell features: tab completion, history, aliases, custom prompts"},"345":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-12","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#what-works","content":"Mouse support in programs that use it"},"346":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-13","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#what-works","content":"Scrollback buffer for reviewing previous output"},"347":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-14","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#what-works","content":"Copy and paste with standard keyboard shortcuts"},"348":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-15","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#remote-terminals","content":"When you select a paired remote device in the sidebar, terminal tabs show that device's sessions. Remote terminals connect over WebSocket and behave identically to local ones — same PTY, same scrollback, same interactive program support."},"349":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-16","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#remote-terminals","content":"From a remote device (like your phone), you can:"},"350":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-17","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#remote-terminals","content":"View and interact with terminals running on the desktop"},"351":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-18","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#remote-terminals","content":"Create new terminal sessions on the desktop"},"352":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-19","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#remote-terminals","content":"Use the same shell with full input support"},"353":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-20","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#remote-terminals","content":"Remote terminal sessions are owned by the desktop. Creating a terminal from your phone actually creates it on the paired desktop — your phone is just the viewer and controller."},"354":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-21","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#working-with-multiple-terminals","content":"The tab bar shows all open terminals. You can:"},"355":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-22","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#working-with-multiple-terminals","content":"**Open** a new terminal with the + button or keyboard shortcut"},"356":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-23","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#working-with-multiple-terminals","content":"**Switch** between terminals by clicking tabs or using keyboard shortcuts"},"357":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-24","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#working-with-multiple-terminals","content":"**Reorder** tabs by dragging"},"358":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-25","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#working-with-multiple-terminals","content":"**Close** a terminal by clicking the tab's X button"},"359":{"id":"/docs/features/terminal-26","page_id":"/docs/features/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/terminal#terminal-within-projects","content":"Terminals can be organized inside Projects. When you create a terminal within a project, it starts in the project's working directory and is grouped with the project's other sessions."},"360":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"page","content":"Voice Input","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input"},"361":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-0","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input","content":"Talk instead of type with built-in speech-to-text."},"362":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-1","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"STT Engines"},"363":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-2","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#native","content":"Native"},"364":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-3","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#whisper","content":"Whisper"},"365":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-4","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#cloud-stt","content":"Cloud STT"},"366":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-5","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#azure-speech","content":"Azure Speech"},"367":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-6","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#how-to-use-it","content":"How to use it"},"368":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-7","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#open-an-agent-chat-tab","content":"Open an Agent Chat tab"},"369":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-8","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#tap-the-microphone-icon","content":"Tap the microphone icon"},"370":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-9","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#speak-your-message","content":"Speak your message"},"371":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-10","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#review-and-send","content":"Review and send"},"372":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-11","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#choosing-an-engine","content":"Choosing an engine"},"373":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-12","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#language-support","content":"Language support"},"374":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-13","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/voice-input#platform-availability","content":"Platform availability"},"375":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-14","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input","content":"Voice Input adds speech-to-text to the agent chat composer. Instead of typing out a detailed prompt, tap the microphone icon and talk. Your speech gets transcribed into text in the composer, ready to send or edit before submitting."},"376":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-15","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input","content":"This is especially useful on mobile devices where typing long prompts is tedious, or when you are describing a problem and just want to think out loud."},"377":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-16","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Gent supports four speech-to-text engines, each with different tradeoffs:"},"378":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-17","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Engine"},"379":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-18","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Runs locally?"},"380":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-19","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Setup"},"381":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-20","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Best for"},"382":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-21","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Native"},"383":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-22","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Yes"},"384":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-23","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"None"},"385":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-24","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Quick dictation with zero setup"},"386":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-25","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Whisper"},"387":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-26","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Yes (after download)"},"388":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-27","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"One-time model download"},"389":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-28","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Offline use, privacy-sensitive work"},"390":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-29","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Cloud STT"},"391":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-30","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"No"},"392":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-31","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"API key"},"393":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-32","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"High accuracy, many languages"},"394":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-33","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Azure Speech"},"395":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-34","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"No"},"396":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-35","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"API key"},"397":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-36","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#stt-engines","content":"Enterprise environments, Azure users"},"398":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-37","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#native","content":"Uses your platform's built-in speech recognition — Siri on Apple devices, Google Speech on Android. No setup required, works immediately. Accuracy depends on your platform's implementation, but it is solid for English and most major languages."},"399":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-38","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#whisper","content":"Runs OpenAI's Whisper model locally on your device. The first time you use it, Gent downloads the model (\\~150MB). After that, everything runs offline — no network requests, no API keys, no data leaving your machine."},"400":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-39","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#whisper","content":"Whisper handles accents and background noise well, and supports dozens of languages out of the box."},"401":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-40","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#cloud-stt","content":"Uses a cloud-based speech-to-text API for transcription. Requires an API key configured in Settings. Offers high accuracy and broad language support, with the tradeoff that audio is sent to an external service for processing."},"402":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-41","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#azure-speech","content":"Microsoft's Azure Speech Services. Requires an Azure subscription and speech resource key. A good fit if you are already in the Azure ecosystem or need enterprise-grade speech recognition with compliance guarantees."},"403":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-42","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#open-an-agent-chat-tab","content":"Voice input works in the agent chat composer — the text field where you type messages to the AI agent."},"404":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-43","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#tap-the-microphone-icon","content":"You will see a mic icon in the composer bar. Tap it to start recording. If this is your first time, Gent may ask for microphone permission."},"405":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-44","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#speak-your-message","content":"Talk naturally. The transcription appears in the composer as you speak. When you are done, tap the mic icon again to stop."},"406":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-45","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#review-and-send","content":"The transcribed text appears in the composer. Edit it if needed, then send it to the agent like any other message."},"407":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-46","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#choosing-an-engine","content":"Open **Settings** and look for the **Speech-to-Text** section. You can select your preferred engine and configure any required credentials. The engine selection persists across sessions."},"408":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-47","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#choosing-an-engine","content":"If you want fully offline voice input with no setup beyond the initial download, Whisper is the way to go. For zero-setup convenience, start with Native and switch later if you need better accuracy."},"409":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-48","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#language-support","content":"All four engines support multiple languages. The available languages depend on the engine:"},"410":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-49","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#language-support","content":"**Native**: Whatever your OS supports — typically 30+ languages on modern devices"},"411":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-50","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#language-support","content":"**Whisper**: 99 languages (full list on OpenAI's Whisper documentation)"},"412":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-51","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#language-support","content":"**Cloud STT**: Varies by provider, typically 50+ languages"},"413":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-52","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#language-support","content":"**Azure Speech**: 100+ languages and variants"},"414":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-53","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#language-support","content":"English variants (US, UK, Australian, etc.) are supported across all engines."},"415":{"id":"/docs/features/voice-input-54","page_id":"/docs/features/voice-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/voice-input#platform-availability","content":"Voice input works on all platforms where Gent runs: macOS, Windows, Linux, Android, and iOS. The Native engine uses platform-specific APIs, so the experience varies slightly — Siri's speech recognition on Apple devices, Google's on Android, and platform speech APIs on desktop. Whisper, Cloud STT, and Azure Speech behave identically across all platforms."},"416":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","type":"page","content":"Web Preview","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/web-preview"},"417":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-0","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview","content":"Preview localhost web apps from any paired device through a built-in reverse proxy."},"418":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-1","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/web-preview#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"419":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-2","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/web-preview#opening-a-web-preview","content":"Opening a web preview"},"420":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-3","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/web-preview#use-cases","content":"Use cases"},"421":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-4","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/web-preview#live-reloading","content":"Live reloading"},"422":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-5","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/web-preview#limitations","content":"Limitations"},"423":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-6","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview","content":"Web Preview lets you view web applications running on one device from another device on your network. If your dev server is running on `localhost:3000` on your Mac, you can see it on your phone without any port forwarding or tunneling setup."},"424":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-7","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#how-it-works","content":"Gent runs a reverse proxy that forwards HTTP requests from the viewing device to the target device's localhost port. The web content is rendered in an embedded browser view within Gent."},"425":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-8","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#how-it-works","content":"This means:"},"426":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-9","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#how-it-works","content":"Your dev server runs normally on localhost"},"427":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-10","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#how-it-works","content":"Gent proxies requests through the paired connection"},"428":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-11","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#how-it-works","content":"The remote device sees the page as if it were on localhost"},"429":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-12","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#how-it-works","content":"No need to find your machine's IP address, no need to bind to `0.0.0.0`, no need for ngrok or similar tools."},"430":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-13","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#opening-a-web-preview","content":"Click &#x2A;*+** in the tab bar"},"431":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-14","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#opening-a-web-preview","content":"Select **Web Preview**"},"432":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-15","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#opening-a-web-preview","content":"Enter the port number (e.g., `3000`, `8080`, `5173`)"},"433":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-16","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#opening-a-web-preview","content":"The preview loads immediately if the server is running on that port."},"434":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-17","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#use-cases","content":"**Mobile testing**: Preview your web app on your actual phone while developing on your desktop"},"435":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-18","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#use-cases","content":"**Cross-device review**: Show a teammate the app running on your machine by having them pair their device"},"436":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-19","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#use-cases","content":"**Remote monitoring**: Check on a running dev server or dashboard from your phone"},"437":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-20","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#use-cases","content":"Web Preview works for any HTTP server running on localhost — React dev servers, Next.js, Vite, Express, Django, Rails, or anything else that serves over HTTP."},"438":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-21","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#live-reloading","content":"If your dev server supports hot module replacement (HMR) or live reload, it works through the preview. Changes you make in your editor trigger the same automatic refresh you would see in a local browser."},"439":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-22","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#limitations","content":"WebSocket connections through the proxy depend on your server's WebSocket configuration"},"440":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-23","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#limitations","content":"HTTPS localhost servers may require additional setup"},"441":{"id":"/docs/features/web-preview-24","page_id":"/docs/features/web-preview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/web-preview#limitations","content":"The embedded browser view has standard web rendering capabilities but is not a full desktop browser"},"442":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session","type":"page","content":"First Session","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-session"},"443":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session-0","