tarted/first-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-session#open-a-terminal","content":"Each terminal is a full PTY session — it runs your actual shell (zsh, bash, fish, etc.) with complete support for colors, cursor movement, and interactive programs like `vim` or `top`."},"460":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-session#working-with-tabs","content":"Tabs appear along the top of the workspace. You can:"},"461":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-session#working-with-tabs","content":"**Reorder** tabs by dragging them"},"462":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-session#working-with-tabs","content":"**Close** a tab by clicking the X or using the keyboard shortcut"},"463":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-session#working-with-tabs","content":"**Create** new tabs with the + button — choose from Terminal, Editor, IDE, Web Preview, or Project"},"464":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-session#working-with-tabs","content":"Each tab type has its own purpose. Terminals run shells, the IDE opens project folders, Web Previews show localhost ports, and Agent Chat connects to AI coding assistants. See Features for details on each."},"465":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session-22","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-session#tab-types-at-a-glance","content":"Tab"},"466":{"id":"/docs/getting-star