her connector you have configured."},"736":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-30","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#mcp-connector-passthrough","content":"Gent handles the MCP config file generation automatically. You do not need to manually configure Claude Code's MCP settings — just enable connectors in Gent's settings and they are available in every agent chat."},"737":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-31","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#tool-approval","content":"Some tool calls require your approval before execution. Gent shows a permission prompt for sensitive operations, letting you review and approve or deny before the agent proceeds."},"738":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-32","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#remote-usage","content":"Claude Code sessions are accessible from paired remote devices. The CLI process runs on the desktop, and the remote device sends input and receives output over the network. You can start a conversation on your Mac and continue interacting with it from your phone."},"739":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-33","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#tips","content":"Use conversation forking when you want to try a different approach"},"740":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-34","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#tips","content":"Enable relevant MCP connectors before starting a chat so the agent has access to your tools from the first message"},"741":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-35","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#tips","content":"Long-running tasks continue working even when you switch t