ading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/overview#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"1182":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview","content":"Gent ships with a full library of integrations built on the &#x2A;*Model Context Protocol (MCP)**. These connectors let your AI agents interact with external services — GitHub, Slack, databases, cloud providers, and more — directly from agent chat."},"1183":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#what-is-mcp","content":"The Model Context Protocol is an open standard for connecting AI assistants to external tools. Each MCP connector runs as a local process that speaks a standardized protocol over stdin/stdout. The connector exposes \"tools\" that the AI agent can call — like creating a GitHub issue, querying a database, or sending a Slack message."},"1184":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-9","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#how-connectors-work-in-gent","content":"When you enable a connector in Gent:"},"1185":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-10","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#how-connectors-work-in-gent","content":"Gent stores your credentials locally (API keys, tokens) in encrypted storage on your device"},"1186":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-11","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#how-connectors-work-in-gent","content":"When you start an agent chat, Gent spawns the connector process and passes it to the CLI as an MCP server"},"1187":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-12","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#how-connectors-work-in-gent","content":"The AI agent discovers the connector's tools and can call them during the conversation"},"1188":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-13","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#how-connectors-work-in-gent","content":"The connector process runs locally on your machine — credentials never leave your device"},"1189":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-14","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#how-connectors-work-in-gent","content":"Gent bundles its own Node.js runtime, so most connectors work out of the box without you needing to install Node.js separately. The bundled runtime handles `npx` commands that connectors use to start."},"1190":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-15","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#first-party-agent-surfaces","content":"Some connectors are built by Gent itself and are always close to the chat workflow:"},"1191":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-16","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#first-party-agent-surfaces","content":"Connector"},"1192":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-17","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#first-party-agent-surfaces","content":"What it gives agents"},"1193":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-18","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#first-party-agent-surfaces","content":"Gent Canvas"},"1194":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-19","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#first-party-agent-surfaces","content":"A sandboxed HTML/JS/CSS renderer beside the chat for web artifacts, charts, demos, and prototypes"},"1195":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-20","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#first-party-agent-surfaces","content":"Gent Forge"},"1196":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-21","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#first-party-agent-surfaces","content":"`/connect anything`: agent-generated MCP servers for products, APIs, websites, and workflows"},"1197":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-22","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#first-party-agent-surfaces","content":"Gent Automations"},"1198":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-23","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#first-party-agent-surfaces","content":"Tools for creating and managing scheduled or triggered agent workflows"},"1199":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-24","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#first-party-agent-surfaces","content":"Gent also bundles Agentic Mobile through Argent, a third-party MCP connector from Software Mansion for controlling, debugging, and profiling iOS and Android apps."},"1200":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-25","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#what-connectors-enable","content":"With connectors, your AI agent can:"},"1201":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-26","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#what-connectors-enable","content":"**Read and write code** on GitHub, GitLab, or Bitbucket"},"1202":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-27","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/overview#what-connectors-enable","content":"**Manage projects** in Linear, Jira, Asana, or Trello"},"1203":{"id":"/docs/integrations/overview-28","page_id":"/docs/integrations/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/o